// Copy to Secrets.xcconfig and fill in. Secrets.xcconfig is gitignored.
//
//     cp Secrets.example.xcconfig Secrets.xcconfig
//
// The anon key is designed to ship in clients and RLS is what actually protects
// the data — but the project URL plus the key is a convenient handle for anyone
// probing the database, and there is no upside to publishing it.
//
// NOTE the missing scheme on the URL. An xcconfig treats `//` as the start of a
// comment, so `https://x.supabase.co` truncates to `https:`. Store the host
// only; SupabaseConfig.fromBundle glues `https://` back on.

ONYX_SUPABASE_URL = your-project.supabase.co
ONYX_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your-anon-key-here
